\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Correlation matrices comparing the daily occurrence between different cloud types using two methods. In the left, the New Method exhibits generally weaker correlations, indicating clearer distinctions between cloud types. In the right, The Old Method shows stronger correlations, suggesting more pronounced interdependencies and potential overlaps between cloud types\relax }}{4}{figure.caption.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:pearson_correlation}{{3}{4}{Correlation matrices comparing the daily occurrence between different cloud types using two methods. In the left, the New Method exhibits generally weaker correlations, indicating clearer distinctions between cloud types. In the right, The Old Method shows stronger correlations, suggesting more pronounced interdependencies and potential overlaps between cloud types\relax }{figure.caption.3}{}}
